<p>Use this dialog box to edit and create bitmap watermarks. Use bitmap 
 files (extension ".bmp") for bitmap watermarks.</p>
<p class="Note">Note:</p>
<ul>
<li><p>To print the same image watermark data using different 
 setting configurations, provide each of the available data combinations 
 with its own image watermark name and register those names in advance.</p></li>
</ul>
<p aria-level="3" class="T2" id="image" role="heading">Bitmap Watermark image</p>
<p>Displays an image of the bitmap as it appears on the page.</p>
<p aria-level="3" class="T2" id="bitmap" role="heading"><span class="Term-Soft">Bitmap:</span></p>
<p>Select a bitmap watermark that you want to edit or delete from the list.</p>
<p aria-level="3" class="T2" id="delete" role="heading"><span class="Term-Soft">Delete</span></p>
<p>Deletes the current watermark.</p>
<p aria-level="2" class="T1" role="heading"><span class="Term-Soft">Edit</span></p>
<p>Configure settings for a bitmap watermark.</p>
<p>Image data files must be 24 bits or lower bitmaps (extension ".bmp").</p>
<p aria-level="3" class="T2" id="name" role="heading"><span class="Term-Soft">Name:</span></p>
<p>Enter a name for the bitmap watermark.</p>
<p aria-level="3" class="T2" id="path" role="heading"><span class="Term-Soft">Path/File Name:</span></p>
<p>Enter a path and file name for the bitmap image file.</p>
<p aria-level="3" class="T2" id="browse" role="heading"><span class="Term-Soft">Browse...</span></p>
<p>Browse for the file you want to use as bitmap watermark.</p>
<p aria-level="3" class="T2" id="size" role="heading"><span class="Term-Soft">Size:</span></p>
<p>Specify a value in this spin box to adjust the size of the bitmap watermark.</p>
<p aria-level="3" class="T2" id="add" role="heading"><span class="Term-Soft">Add</span></p>
<p>Adds an edited watermark as a new bitmap watermark to the list.</p>
<p aria-level="3" class="T2" id="update" role="heading"><span class="Term-Soft">Update</span></p>
<p>Saves the changes after editing a bitmap watermark.</p>
<p aria-level="3" class="T2" id="position" role="heading"><span class="Term-Soft">Position:</span></p>
<p>Select a printing position where you want to print the watermark.</p>
<p aria-level="3" class="T2" id="firstpage" role="heading"><span class="Term-Soft">First Page Only</span></p>
<p>Select the check box to print the bitmap watermark on the first page 
 only.</p>
<p aria-level="3" class="T2" id="opaque" role="heading"><span class="Term-Soft">Opaque</span></p>
<p>Select the check box to make the bitmap watermark opaque. The image 
 under the watermark will not be visible.</p>
<p aria-level="3" class="T2" id="repeat" role="heading"><span class="Term-Soft">Repeat</span></p>
<p>Prints bitmap watermarks repeatedly from the top left of the page.</p>
<p aria-level="3" class="T2" id="original" role="heading"><span class="Term-Soft">Per Original Page</span></p>
<p>Select the check box to print the bitmap watermark on each original 
 page even when <span class="Term-Soft">Layout</span> or <span class="Term-Soft">Booklet</span> 
 setting is applied.</p>
<p aria-level="3" class="T2" id="ok" role="heading"><span class="Term-Soft">OK</span></p>
<p>Saves the changes and closes the dialog box.</p>
<p aria-level="3" class="T2" id="cancel" role="heading"><span class="Term-Soft">Cancel</span></p>
<p>Closes the dialog box without saving any changes.</p>
<p aria-level="3" class="T2" id="help" role="heading"><span class="Term-Soft">Help</span></p>
<p>Displays Help for the dialog box opened.</p>
